WEBVTT

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:02.176
Those are super fun,
and, actually, not that hard.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.792
You know, at the very root
of that, see, Caspers,

00:05:04.816 --> 00:05:06.385
see how you throw it?

00:05:07.512 --> 00:05:09.991
Simple as that, right? No biggie.

00:05:10.015 --> 00:05:13.483
And your front foot,
the way it grabs it --

00:05:14.761 --> 00:05:17.528
I'd seen someone slide
on the back of the board like that,

00:05:17.552 --> 00:05:19.474
and I was like, "How can I get it over?"

00:05:19.498 --> 00:05:21.204
Because that had not yet been done.

00:05:21.228 --> 00:05:24.111
And then it dawned on me,
and here's part of what I'm saying.

00:05:24.135 --> 00:05:26.328
I had an infrastructure.
I had this deep layer,

00:05:26.352 --> 00:05:28.780
where it was like, oh my gosh,
it's just your foot.

00:05:28.804 --> 00:05:30.876
It's just the way
you throw your board over.